    probes: 'END-OF-LEVEL TRIGGERS: clear each level by real input where practical (cmd allowed only to reach the boss quickly — say where) and verify the clear trigger fires exactly once in every edge case: Stag and last add dying on the same tick, the party wiping on the same tick as the clear, Esc/pause, Enter, Quit to Lobby and a save request pressed during the transition card, alt-tab / hidden tab during the transition, 4x CPU throttle. MEMORY BETWEEN AUTOMATIC LOADS: sample at the first controllable frame of L1, L2, L3 and again across 3 back-to-back full campaigns (and after Quit to Lobby mid-level): renderer.info.memory geometries + textures, renderer.info.programs length, JS heap after a forced GC (CDP HeapProfiler.collectGarbage + Runtime.getHeapUsage), entityCount, event-bus listener count, VFX/decal/particle pool sizes, DOM node count, live audio voices/AudioNodes — report tables; any monotonic growth across campaigns or level-specific objects surviving into the next level is a must-fix. CARRY/RESET RULES: diff state at every transition against the CAMPAIGN MODEL table (skills, sockets, bench, Glint, HP restored, downed revived, statuses and cooldowns cleared, zero enemies/projectiles/zones/hazards/decals/telegraphs/numerals carried). NO BLACK SCREENS OR LOADING LOOPS: sample frames every 50-100 ms across each transition (screenshots + analyzer luma, plus rAF gaps): report max consecutive near-black frames, longest frame gap, time from the killing blow to the first controllable frame of the next level; the level index must advance exactly once per clear, never loop back, never stall on the card; repeat on the production build (npm run build + vite preview on your port). LOBBY LOCKING: locked levels unselectable by keyboard, mouse and mocked gamepad; unlock persists across reload; a Level-N start plays N -> final. Also: Begin Run always starts Level 1; final clear returns to camp automatically; defeat returns to camp; Quit to Lobby from pause mid-level returns cleanly; save mid-campaign and after a transition, reload, Continue resumes the right level with the carried build; a 2-client network session follows L1 -> L2 in sync.',
